-- C-STYLE LOOP ------------------------------------------------- main.kl  K0926

`for (let i = 0; i < n; i++)` and `for i in range(n)` come from other languages. Kalam loops over a range written `0..n`.

3│     for (var i = 0; i < items.len(); i += 1):
       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

Try: ` i in 0..items.len()`

Help: Write `for i in 0..n:`. Use `0..=n` to include `n` itself. `kalam fix` does this for you.

Learn more: kalam explain K0926
